## Background Job Performance (Hangfire)

### Job Design Rules
- Keep jobs idempotent — safe to retry on failure
- Use `IDbContextFactory<CoreContext>` in jobs (not scoped DbContext)
- Set appropriate `[AutomaticRetry(Attempts = 3)]` with backoff
- Time-box long-running jobs — use `CancellationToken` and check it periodically
- Log job start/end times with Serilog for duration monitoring

### Known Issue
`GetScheduleTaskByNameQuery` runs indefinitely in background — potential causes:
- EF Core infinite retry on empty `ScheduledJobs` table
- Circular DI resolution in request pipeline
- Missing CancellationToken propagation

Resolution approach: Add targeted logging, set query timeout, validate DI registration.

## Observability

### Health Checks
```csharp
builder.Services.AddHealthChecks()
    .AddDbContextCheck<CoreContext>("database")
    .AddCheck("hangfire", () =>
    {
        // Verify Hangfire connection
        return HealthCheckResult.Healthy();
    });

app.MapHealthChecks("/health", new HealthCheckOptions
{
    ResponseWriter = UIResponseWriter.WriteHealthCheckUIResponse
});
```

### Structured Logging (Serilog)
```csharp
// GOOD: Structured properties for searchability
Log.Information("User {UserId} logged in from {IpAddress}", userId, ipAddress);

// BAD: String interpolation destroys structure
Log.Information($"User {userId} logged in from {ipAddress}");
```

### Key Metrics to Track
- Request duration (P50, P95, P99)
- Active SignalR circuits count
- Database query duration by operation
- Cache hit/miss ratio
- Hangfire job queue depth and execution time
- Memory usage (working set, GC collections)
- Error rate by endpoint/component

